    "problem_statement": "Async callbacks not working in DSPy\n\nWhen using async functions with callbacks in DSPy, the callbacks are not being triggered. This affects both `acall` methods in `BaseLM` and `Module` classes.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n```python\nimport dspy\nimport time\n\nclass MyCallback(dspy.BaseCallback):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.calls = []\n        \n    def on_module_start(self, call_id, instance, inputs):\n        self.calls.append({\n            'handler': 'on_module_start',\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'instance': instance,\n            'inputs': inputs\n        })\n        \n    def on_module_end(self, call_id, outputs, exception):\n        self.calls.append({\n            'handler': 'on_module_end',\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'outputs': outputs,\n            'exception': exception\n        })\n\nclass AsyncModule(dspy.Module):\n    async def forward(self, x):\n        return x * 2\n\n# Set up callback\ncallback = MyCallback()\ndspy.settings.configure(callbacks=[callback])\n\n# Create module\nmodule = AsyncModule()\n\n# Run async call\nimport asyncio\nresult = asyncio.run(module.acall(5))\n\n# Check if callbacks were triggered\nprint(f\"Result: {result}\")\nprint(f\"Callback calls: {len(callback.calls)}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: The callback's `on_module_start` and `on_module_end` methods should be called, and `len(callback.calls)` should be 2.\n\nActual behavior: No callbacks are triggered, and `len(callback.calls)` is 0, even though the async call itself works correctly.\n\nThis issue affects all async operations that should have callback support."
